 "observations": [
  "col_left L1, L3, L7, L14, L20-L22, L24-L26: the H of «Ḥammād», «Ḥammāditae», «Ḥamzah», «Ḥarrānenses», «Ḥarrān», «al-Ḥasan» (four times) and «al-Ḥaṣṣār» has its dot below; the dots under the s of «al-Iṣfahānī», «al-Khaṣīb» (twice), «*ḥāṣṣah*» and «al-Ḥaṣṣār», and under the h of «*ḥanīf*» and «*ḥāṣṣah*», are printed.",
  "col_left L3: a speck about 10 points above the baseline before «{sc:xxvi}» is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L6, L11, L28: «*al-han‘ah*», «*al-haq‘ah*» and «*haylāǵ*» are printed with plain h (no dot below); the first two have the sign of ‘ayn.",
  "col_left L10: the P of «Pet.» has a hooked stroke joined to the left of its stem at mid height, a flaw of the sort; read P. A speck (1.1 by 1.1 points) after «226.» is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L18: after «b» five points are printed at equal distances (5.1-5.8 points apart); a speck above the ū of «Hārūn», 9-11 points above the baseline, is not transcribed. The Z of «az-Zayyāt» is printed broken.",
  "col_left L19: a speck (0.6 by 0.6 point) under the d of «ar-Rashīd», 2.9 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L20-L22: the marks over the last i of «al-Khaṣīb» (twice), «al-Marrākushī», «al-Qummī» and «an-Naysābūrī» are bars (2.3-2.4 by 1.0-1.2 points); the r of «an-Naysābūrī» is printed broken, like ı and r.",
  "col_left L34: the tail of the y of «Henry» is printed broken; its end stands apart below the letter like a round dot (1.4 by 1.7 points); not a dot below.",
  "col_left L37: the second e of «fragmenta» is printed without its bar, like c.",
  "col_left L38, L39: the guillemets around «sapiens» are printed as small solid wedges, as on pp. 366, 370, 374, 377, 381, 382, 384 and 386.",
  "col_left L43: «β» is Greek.",
  "col_left L46, col_right L1: the entry Hermes Trismegistus goes on at the head of the right column.",
  "col_right L1, L2: the d of «*al-‘arḍ*» has its dot below, in both lines; the word has the sign of ‘ayn.",
  "col_right L6: the mark over the last i of «al-Akfānī» is a bar.",
  "col_right L8, L10: «*hiǵrah*» and «*haylāǵ*» are printed with ǵ, Nallino's sign for jīm, and plain h.",
  "col_right L9, L12, L22: the h of «*ḥikmah*», «*al-ḥimarāni*» and «*ḥiṣṣat*» has its dot below; both s of «*ḥiṣṣat*» have theirs. A speck (1.1 by 1.1 points) after «8.» in L9 is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L12: «*al-ḥimarāni*» is printed with a macron over the second a only (the same word on p. 378 has macrons over both a); transcribed as printed. The last i is dotted (the dual ending). «γ» and «δ» are Greek; the l of «al» is printed broken.",
  "col_right L13: «*Ibbarkhos*» is printed in italics; «Abrachis» upright.",
  "col_right L31, L36, L39, L41: the e of «et» (L31) and the o of «horae» (L36), «noctis» (L39) and the second o of «quomodo» (L41) are printed broken, open at one side; read e and o.",
  "col_right L36, L37: «*sā‘āt*» has bars over both a and the sign of ‘ayn; «*at-taqwīm*» has a bar over the i."
 ],
